'''''Flexitrichum''''' is a genus of [[Peristome#In_mosses|haplolepideous]] [[moss]]es ([[Dicranidae]]) in the family '''Flexitrichaceae'''.<ref name=Tropicos/><ref name=Goffinet-2020-web>{{cite web |last1=Goffinet |first1=B. |first2=W.R. |last2=Buck |title=Classification of extant moss genera  |website=Classification of the Bryophyta |date=31 March 2020 |url=http://bryology.uconn.edu/classification/#DICRANIDAE |access-date=8 April 2020}}</ref><ref name=Fedosov-2016>{{cite journal|last1=Fedosov|first1=Vladimir E.|last2=Fedorova|first2=Alina V.|last3=Fedosov|first3=Alexander E.|last4=Ignatov|first4=Michael S.|title=Phylogenetic inference and peristome evolution in haplolepideous mosses, focusing on Pseudoditrichaceae and Ditrichaceaes. l.|journal=Botanical Journal of the Linnean Society|volume=181|issue=2|year=2016|pages=139–155|issn=0024-4074|doi=10.1111/boj.12408|doi-access=free}}</ref>

==Species==
The genus contains two species:<ref name=Tropicos>{{BioRef|Tropicos|title=''Flexitrichum'' Ignatov & Fedosov|id=100444531|access-date=9 April 2020}}</ref><ref name=Fedosov-2016/>

*''[[Flexitrichum flexicaule]]'' {{small|(Schwägr.) Ignatov & Fedosov}}
*''[[Flexitrichum gracile]]'' {{small|(Mitt.) Ignatov & Fedosov}}

These species were previously considered members of the genus ''[[Ditrichum]]'' in the family [[Ditrichaceae]], either as two species or both included in ''Ditrichum flexicaule''.<ref name=Fedosov-2016/><ref name=WFO>{{BioRef|WFO|title=''Flexitrichum'' Hampe|id=4000012284|access-date=9 April 2020}}</ref>

